  },
  "narration": [
    {
      "id": "s7_01",
      "text": "It is also important to see machine learning as a workflow, not just a collection of algorithms.",
      "emphasis": "workflow"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7_02",
      "text": "The process usually begins with data collection. We gather the information we need.",
      "emphasis": "data collection"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7_03",
      "text": "But raw data is rarely clean. It often contains missing values, noise, and inconsistencies.",
      "emphasis": "rarely clean"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7_04",
      "text": "So the next step is preprocessing. Here we clean the data, organize it, and transform it into a form the model can use.",
      "emphasis": "preprocessing"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7_05",
      "text": "Then comes model selection and training. We choose a model, train it on the data, and let it learn the pattern.",
      "emphasis": "training"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7_06",
      "text": "After that comes evaluation. This is where we test how well the model performs on new data.",
      "emphasis": "evaluation"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7_07",
      "text": "This step matters because a model can sometimes do well on training data but fail on unseen data. That problem is called overfitting.",
      "emphasis": "overfitting"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7_08",
      "text": "Finally, we move to deployment and improvement. A model is usually not the end of the story.",
      "emphasis": "deployment and improvement"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7_09",
      "text": "Once it is used in the real world, we monitor its performance and improve it over time.",
      "emphasis": "improve it over time"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7_10",
      "text": "So machine learning is not a one-step process. It is a loop: data, preprocessing, training, evaluation, improvement.",
      "emphasis": "loop"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7_11",
      "text": "That loop is the real workflow of the field.",
      "emphasis": "real workflow"
    }
  ],
